e MyD88-dependent signal...", "text": "All TLRs, except for TLR3, employ the MyD88-dependent signaling pathway. Autosomal recessive MyD88 deficiency predispose affected patients to recurrent pyogenic bacterial infection due to abolished TLR-mediated cytokine responses of the blood cells (von Bernuth H et al. 2008; Currie AJ et al. 2004). Here we describe several natural loss-of-function MyD88 variants (E52del, L93P, E65del, S34T) that showed severely reduced NFkB activation in human cell-based assays due to reduced homooligomerization and IRAK4 interaction, the two crucial events in the assembly of the Myddosome complex (George J et al. 2011; Nagpal K et al. 2011; Yamamoto T et al. 2014).", "literatureReference": [5602589, 2428864, 5602389, 5602701, {"dbId": 5602438, "displayName": "Natural loss-of-function mutation of myeloid differentiation protein 88 disrupts its ability to form Myddosomes", "title": "Natural loss-of-function mutation of myeloid differentiation protein 88 disrupts its ability to form Myddosomes", "journal": "J. Biol. Chem.", "pages": "11875-82", "pubMedIdentifier": 21325272, "volume": 286, "year": 2011, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21325272", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "updateTrackers": [{"dbId": 9779922, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [FailedReaction:5602383] Defective MyD88 does not oligomerize within the activated TLR2/4 complex - v64:[add_removeInput]", "action": ["add_removeInput"], "updatedInstance": [5602383], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}], "isChimeric": false, "systematicName": "Defective MyD88 variants do not bind IRAK4, Activated TLR1:2 or TLR 2:6 heterodimers or TLR4 homodimer", "category": "transition"